Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::the_header_checks_before_the_crc_are_total`.

The defect: the header size is checked against its lower bound only, so a header that declares
itself larger than its block is accepted, and the CRC step that follows slices past the block's
end and panics on hostile input.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(size <= block.len())`, on any header that passes the other
checks and declares a size above 512.
diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/header.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/header.rs
